490-491	600,479,1324,1173 - 1224,470,1330,948 - 1250,945,1296,974	490. Flowering branchlet of Leatherwood. 491. Branch with foliage and fruit.	One block: 491, a thick jointed branch with oval leaves and a cluster of three oblong berries; across it, 490, a leafy branchlet hung with small drooping funnel-shaped flowers.
492	1219,477,1346,938 - 1219,620,1226,730	492. A flower, magnified.	A single flower: a narrow tubular calyx on a short stalk, with eight stamens and a long curved style protruding from its mouth.
493	1401,509,1669,1169	493. Same, more magnified, the calyx laid open.	The calyx tube slit and spread flat, showing the eight long stamens attached inside it and the pistil with its oval ovary and slender style.
